Source: https://github.com/zarazhangrui/frontend-slides at
9906a34d640d2111f724544cbc50f7f130569ae1.

What is adapted from it here: the slides skill
(internal/controlplane/clientcli/skills/slides/): its SKILL.md, html-template.md,
STYLE_PRESETS.md, animation-patterns.md, viewport-base.css and
scripts/extract-pptx.py. Changed: a deck is shown with `hypomnema artifact show`
and revised with `--id`, in place of Vercel (scripts/deploy.sh) and `open`; the
PDF export (scripts/export-pdf.sh) is left out; fonts are system font stacks in
place of Fontshare and Google Fonts; inline editing and its localStorage are left
out; extract-pptx.py runs with the Bots' documents environment and its images are
kept in a deck folder beside index.html; files are named where the skill is
installed, ~/.agents/skills/slides, and the name is `slides`. Left out: the
Claude Code plugin copy (plugins/, .claude-plugin/), README.md and the bold
template pack (bold-template-pack/), whose templates load their fonts and charts
from the network.

The system font stacks in STYLE_PRESETS.md are from Modern Font Stacks
(https://github.com/system-fonts/modern-font-stacks at
76f973110be618cb6a443abc4ae5964182d1fd58), dedicated to the public domain under
CC0 1.0.
